Now comes the correction. The one-sided states $\psi_L$ and $\psi_R$ are neither symmetric nor antisymmetric, so they cannot be exact eigenstates of the full Hamiltonian. They are only good approximate states when the barrier is high. The true eigenstates are the symmetric and antisymmetric combinations, $\begin{aligned}
\psi_+ &= \frac{\psi_L+\psi_R}{\sqrt{2}},\\
\psi_- &= \frac{\psi_L-\psi_R}{\sqrt{2}}.\end{aligned}$ Using the notation that will remain on the board, label their energies by $\begin{aligned}
H\psi_+ &= (E_1-\epsilon)\psi_+,\\
H\psi_- &= (E_1+\epsilon)\psi_-.\end{aligned}$ The total splitting is therefore $\Delta E = (E_1+\epsilon)-(E_1-\epsilon)=2\epsilon .$

