The inverse relations are $\begin{aligned}
\psi_L &= \frac{\psi_+ + \psi_-}{\sqrt{2}},\\
\psi_R &= \frac{\psi_+ - \psi_-}{\sqrt{2}}.\end{aligned}$ So an initially left-localized state is $\psi(0)=\psi_L=\frac{\psi_+ + \psi_-}{\sqrt{2}}.$ It is not an energy eigenstate, and therefore it must evolve nontrivially.

